  "body": "## Why\n\nThe floating-player **pin** misbehaved: the button didn't feel like it toggled, and — the real complaint — **the titlebar never came back after unpinning** (the window stayed effectively pinned: no titlebar, and it dragged by the video body).\n\n## Root cause\n\nTwo layers, found by tracing both sides of the windowless-WebView2 seam and then capturing the live SSE stream:\n\n1. **The actual \"titlebar doesn't return\" bug is in status delivery, not the pin logic.** The control server streams status over SSE through **tiny_http 0.12**, which buffers the response in a **1024-byte `BufWriter` and never flushes a streaming body**. A small status frame sits unsent until enough *following* bytes overflow the buffer — so when you unpin a **paused** video (no playback frames follow), the host's `window_on_top:false` never reaches the overlay. The host genuinely unpinned (`/status` = false, window not topmost) but the overlay never heard it.\n2. **Pin state was split across three stores that could drift and never re-sync** (`onTopRef` for command direction, echoed `status.window_on_top` for the button highlight, host `is_on_top` for hit-testing), and the button highlight lagged a full round-trip so a click felt dead.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`webserver.rs` (the cure for the titlebar):** when the SSE stream would idle after a frame, emit a \u003e1 KiB SSE comment (clients ignore `:`-prefixed lines) to overflow the BufWriter and force the frame to the socket at once. Verified with a live capture: the unpin's `false` now arrives ~150ms after the click instead of never. New regression test locks the idle-flush path.\n\n**`App.tsx`:** one optimistic value drives both the button highlight (instant) and the next-command direction; rolled back to host truth on a failed command; surface-drag gated on the host-confirmed `window_on_top` so the window always has exactly one drag handle.\n\n**`compositor.rs`:** fullscreen-exit re-applies topmost from live `is_on_top` (titlebar can't vanish forever); pin-entry clears `WS_MAXIMIZE` before the aspect snap (resize borders survive); `WM_GETMINMAXINFO` floors the window above its own chrome; pin-mode control bar reliably reveals after a modal move; pre-pin rect persisted instead of the aspect-snapped one.\n\n**Docs:** added the \"Pin toggle: one click, one command\" contract section that `desktop-shell.md` already linked to; refreshed ADR-0001.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo test -p shows-desktop`: 21/21 pass (incl. new `status_stream_flushes_idle_frame_with_oversized_comment`)\n- Frontend `tsc` clean\n- Live SSE capture before/after confirms the unpin `false` now delivers promptly while paused\n- Manually verified end-to-end by the user: pause → pin → unpin restores the titlebar\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
